These values have different jobs:

Value	Purpose
image.tag	Determines which Docker image Kubernetes runs
config.appVersion	Passed to the FastAPI application through the ConfigMap
Chart.yaml appVersion	Helm metadata and labels; usually informational

However, manually repeating the same version creates a risk:

image.tag:        1.0.2
config.appVersion: 1.0.1  ← accidental mismatch

A better design is to make the image tag the single source of truth. In configmap.yaml, change:

APP_VERSION: {{ .Values.config.appVersion | quote }}

to:

APP_VERSION: {{ .Values.image.tag | quote }}

Then remove this from values.yaml:

appVersion: "1.0.1"

Afterward, every release requires changing only:

image:
  tag: "1.0.2"

